{
  "model": "claude-sonnet-5",
  "max_tokens": 8000,
  "system": "You are a Senior Microsoft Solution Architect and Enterprise Proposal Writer with 15+ years of experience drafting formal Statements of Work for Microsoft Gold Partners. Return ONLY one valid JSON object. Never return markdown. Never return code fences. Never return explanations outside the JSON. Never return arrays or nested objects. Every property value MUST be a single string. Use '\n• ' inside strings for bullet lists. Write in formal, enterprise, client-facing business English. Each section must be substantive, detailed, and written in complete, professional sentences — avoid short or generic phrases. The response MUST start with '{' and end with '}'.",
  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Generate a detailed, production-grade Microsoft Statement of Work (SOW) suitable for a formal client-facing document. You MUST include all 14 keys listed below, in this exact order, with no omissions. DocumentHeader must never be empty. Each section should be thorough and written with multiple full sentences (not short fragments) to reflect a professional consulting deliverable.

Partner Code: @{triggerBody()['text']}
Client Company: @{triggerBody()['text_1']}
Client Email: @{triggerBody()['text_2']}
Primary Contact: @{triggerBody()['text_3']}
Service Area: @{triggerBody()['text_4']}
Support Hours: @{triggerBody()['text_5']}
Project Duration: @{triggerBody()['text_6']}
Microsoft Environment: @{triggerBody()['text_7']}
Engagement Brief: @{triggerBody()['text_8']}
Pricing Model: @{triggerBody()['text_9']}
Payment Terms: @{triggerBody()['text_10']}

Create these sections with the following depth requirements:

DocumentHeader: one line containing the document title, client company name, partner code, and project duration, formatted as a single readable string.
ExecutiveSummary: a rich paragraph (120-180 words) summarizing the engagement, business context, and value proposition.
Objectives: one string containing five detailed bullet points separated by \n• , each bullet being a full sentence describing a specific, measurable objective.
ScopeOfServices: one string containing six detailed bullet points separated by \n• , covering technical, functional, and support scope comprehensively.
PhasedRoadmap: one string containing four bullet points separated by \n• , each describing a project phase with approximate duration and key activities.
GovernanceModel: a detailed paragraph (80-120 words) describing meeting cadence, escalation paths, reporting structure, and stakeholder roles.
Assumptions: one string containing five bullet points separated by \n• , covering technical, resource, and client-dependency assumptions.
AcceptanceCriteria: one string containing five bullet points separated by \n• , describing measurable, verifiable completion criteria.
OutOfScope: one string containing five bullet points separated by \n• , explicitly excluding adjacent services to prevent scope creep.
ChangeControl: a detailed paragraph (80-120 words) explaining the change request process, approval workflow, and impact assessment procedure.
RisksAndMitigations: one string containing four bullet points separated by \n• , each describing a specific risk paired with its mitigation strategy.
CommercialTerms: a detailed paragraph (80-120 words) covering pricing structure, invoicing schedule, currency, and payment terms.
Deliverables: one string containing six bullet points separated by \n• , listing concrete, tangible deliverables with brief descriptions.
DocumentAuthorisation: a formal paragraph (60-100 words) describing signatory requirements, effective date clause, and mutual agreement language.

Return EXACTLY this JSON object structure with the values filled in:
{
"DocumentHeader":"",
"ExecutiveSummary":"",
"Objectives":"",
"ScopeOfServices":"",
"PhasedRoadmap":"",
